IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ssc-core`
IMPORT `ssc9-sch5`
IMPORT `ssc9-sch5-w`

-- Tests for ssc9-sch5-w.l4 (Schedule 5, paragraphs 3C to 9). Expected values are written by hand from the text, beside each assertion.

§ `Tests -- Schedule 5 paragraphs 3C to 9`

§§ `Fixtures`

`sch 5 test a widow who attained pensionable age in 2005` MEANS Person WITH
    `date of birth` IS Date 1 1 1940
    `sex` IS Woman
    `marital status` IS `widowed or a surviving civil partner`
    `date of attaining pensionable age` IS Date 1 1 2005

`sch 5 test a widow who attained pensionable age on 5 April 1979` MEANS Person WITH
    `date of birth` IS Date 1 1 1917
    `sex` IS Woman
    `marital status` IS `widowed or a surviving civil partner`
    `date of attaining pensionable age` IS Date 5 4 1979

`sch 5 test a widow who attained pensionable age on 6 April 1979` MEANS Person WITH
    `date of birth` IS Date 1 1 1917
    `sex` IS Woman
    `marital status` IS `widowed or a surviving civil partner`
    `date of attaining pensionable age` IS Date 6 4 1979

`sch 5 test a widower` MEANS Person WITH
    `date of birth` IS Date 1 1 1940
    `sex` IS Man
    `marital status` IS `widowed or a surviving civil partner`
    `date of attaining pensionable age` IS Date 1 1 2005

`sch 5 test a deceased husband` MEANS Person WITH
    `date of birth` IS Date 1 1 1938
    `sex` IS Man
    `marital status` IS `married`
    `date of attaining pensionable age` IS Date 1 1 2003

`sch 5 test a deceased wife` MEANS Person WITH
    `date of birth` IS Date 1 1 1938
    `sex` IS Woman
    `marital status` IS `married`
    `date of attaining pensionable age` IS Date 1 1 1998

`sch 5 test a pension with every named increase` MEANS `sch 5 Weekly pension` WITH
    `the pension apart from the increases named in this Schedule` IS 100
    `the increase under section 47(1)` IS 5
    `the increase under paragraph 4` IS 3
    `the increases under paragraphs 5 to 6A` IS 2
    `the increase under section 83A` IS 7
    `the increase under section 85` IS 11
    `the graduated retirement benefit` IS 13

§§ `Paragraph 8(4) and 3C(1)`

-- Expected: a Category B pension earned by W's contributions does not satisfy the condition (false); any other pension: not spoken to.
#ASSERT `sch 5 para 8(4) the conditions in paragraphs 3C(1)(c) and 4(1)(a) are satisfied by S’s pension` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `sch 5 para 8(4) the conditions in paragraphs 3C(1)(c) and 4(1)(a) are satisfied by S’s pension` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- 3C(1)(d): deferred 1 Jan 2024 to the day before death. Death 1 Jan 2025 gives 12 months exactly; death 31 Dec 2024 is a day short (the predicate named for the limit answers FALSE short of it).
#ASSERT `sch 5 para 3C(1)(d) S’s entitlement was deferred throughout the 12 months` (Date 1 1 2024) (Date 1 1 2025) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 5 para 3C(1)(d) S’s entitlement was deferred throughout the 12 months` (Date 1 1 2024) (Date 31 12 2024) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `sch 5 para 3C(1)(d) S’s entitlement was deferred throughout the 12 months` (Date 1 2 2025) (Date 1 1 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Fork F1: deferment from 29 Feb 2024, death on 28 Feb 2025 (last day 27 Feb) is the one day the readings differ: NOTHING; death 1 Mar 2025 is 12 months on both.
#ASSERT `sch 5 para 3C(1)(d) S’s entitlement was deferred throughout the 12 months` (Date 29 2 2024) (Date 28 2 2025) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `sch 5 para 3C(1)(d) S’s entitlement was deferred throughout the 12 months` (Date 29 2 2024) (Date 1 3 2025) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- 3C(1): all of (a), (b), (c) and (d) -> applies; any one missing, or the Category B exclusion, or under 12 months -> NOTHING.
#ASSERT `sch 5 para 3C(1) this paragraph applies` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE (Date 1 1 2024) (Date 1 1 2025) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 5 para 3C(1) this paragraph applies` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE (Date 1 1 2024) (Date 1 1 2025) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `sch 5 para 3C(1) this paragraph applies` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE (Date 1 1 2024) (Date 1 1 2025) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `sch 5 para 3C(1) this paragraph applies` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE (Date 1 1 2024) (Date 1 1 2025) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `sch 5 para 3C(1) this paragraph applies` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE (Date 1 1 2024) (Date 1 1 2025) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `sch 5 para 3C(1) this paragraph applies` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE (Date 1 1 2024) (Date 31 12 2024) EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `Paragraph 3C(2), (3), (5)`

-- The duty, prescribed period 28 days. Read by eye: an election on day 12 -> FULFILLED; a lapse to day 29 -> FULFILLED (3C(3) deems the lump sum).
#TRACE `sch 5 para 3C(2) the election duty` 28 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `sch 5 W the widow, widower or surviving civil partner` DOES `sch 5 W makes an election` `sch 5 para 3C(2)(a) an election that paragraph 4 (the increase of pension) applies` AT 12
#TRACE `sch 5 para 3C(2) the election duty` 28 AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 29)
-- 3C(3): no election in time -> the (b) lump-sum election; an election made stands.
#ASSERT `sch 5 para 3C(3) the election that is treated as made` NOTHING EQUALS `sch 5 para 3C(2)(b) an election that paragraph 7A (the lump sum) applies`
#ASSERT `sch 5 para 3C(3) the election that is treated as made` (JUST `sch 5 para 3C(2)(a) an election that paragraph 4 (the increase of pension) applies`) EQUALS `sch 5 para 3C(2)(a) an election that paragraph 4 (the increase of pension) applies`
-- 3C(5): the lump-sum election does not affect paragraphs 5 to 6A (false); the other election is not spoken to.
#ASSERT `sch 5 para 3C(5) the election affects the application of paragraphs 5 to 6A` `sch 5 para 3C(2)(b) an election that paragraph 7A (the lump sum) applies` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `sch 5 para 3C(5) the election affects the application of paragraphs 5 to 6A` `sch 5 para 3C(2)(a) an election that paragraph 4 (the increase of pension) applies` EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `Paragraph 4`

-- 4(5): death before 6 April 1979 and W of pensionable age before that date (5 April 1979) -> the paragraph does not apply.
#ASSERT `sch 5 para 4(5) this paragraph does not apply` (Date 5 4 1979) `sch 5 test a widow who attained pensionable age on 5 April 1979` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 5 para 4(5) this paragraph does not apply` (Date 6 4 1979) `sch 5 test a widow who attained pensionable age on 5 April 1979` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `sch 5 para 4(5) this paragraph does not apply` (Date 5 4 1979) `sch 5 test a widow who attained pensionable age on 6 April 1979` EQUALS NOTHING
-- 4(1)(a): S was entitled with an increase under this Schedule -> applies.
#ASSERT `sch 5 para 4(1) this paragraph applies` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE (Date 1 1 2024) (Date 1 1 2025) NOTHING `sch 5 test a widow who attained pensionable age in 2005` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- 4(5) takes the paragraph away: death 1 Jan 1979, W of pensionable age on 5 April 1979 -> does not apply, even on limb (a).
#ASSERT `sch 5 para 4(1) this paragraph applies` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE (Date 1 1 1970) (Date 1 1 1979) NOTHING `sch 5 test a widow who attained pensionable age on 5 April 1979` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- A Category B pension earned by W's contributions does not satisfy 4(1)(a); with nothing else, NOTHING.
#ASSERT `sch 5 para 4(1) this paragraph applies` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE (Date 1 1 2024) (Date 1 1 2025) NOTHING `sch 5 test a widow who attained pensionable age in 2005` EQUALS NOTHING
-- 4(1)(b): 3C applies and W elected the increase -> applies; W elected the lump sum -> not this paragraph (NOTHING).
#ASSERT `sch 5 para 4(1) this paragraph applies` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE (Date 1 1 2024) (Date 1 1 2025) (JUST `sch 5 para 3C(2)(a) an election that paragraph 4 (the increase of pension) applies`) `sch 5 test a widow who attained pensionable age in 2005` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 5 para 4(1) this paragraph applies` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE (Date 1 1 2024) (Date 1 1 2025) (JUST `sch 5 para 3C(2)(b) an election that paragraph 7A (the lump sum) applies`) `sch 5 test a widow who attained pensionable age in 2005` EQUALS NOTHING
-- 4(1)(c): 3C would apply but for (d): deferred when S died but for under 12 months (1 Jan 2024 to 30 Dec 2024).
#ASSERT `sch 5 para 4(1) this paragraph applies` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE (Date 1 1 2024) (Date 31 12 2024) NOTHING `sch 5 test a widow who attained pensionable age in 2005` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- The 29 February fork day: neither (b) nor (c) can be told -> NOTHING.
#ASSERT `sch 5 para 4(1) this paragraph applies` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE (Date 29 2 2024) (Date 28 2 2025) NOTHING `sch 5 test a widow who attained pensionable age in 2005` EQUALS NOTHING
-- W not entitled: NOTHING.
#ASSERT `sch 5 para 4(1) this paragraph applies` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE (Date 1 1 2024) (Date 1 1 2025) NOTHING `sch 5 test a widow who attained pensionable age in 2005` EQUALS NOTHING
-- 4(1A) and (3), basic 10 and additional 6: married, death 5 Oct 2002 -> 16; 6 Oct 2002 -> 10 + 3 = 13; civil partner 4 Dec 2005 -> 16; 5 Dec 2005 -> 13.
#ASSERT `sch 5 para 4(1A) the amount by which the rate of W’s pension is increased` (Date 5 10 2002) FALSE 10 6 EQUALS 16
#ASSERT `sch 5 para 4(1A) the amount by which the rate of W’s pension is increased` (Date 6 10 2002) FALSE 10 6 EQUALS 13
#ASSERT `sch 5 para 4(1A) the amount by which the rate of W’s pension is increased` (Date 4 12 2005) TRUE 10 6 EQUALS 16
#ASSERT `sch 5 para 4(1A) the amount by which the rate of W’s pension is increased` (Date 5 12 2005) TRUE 10 6 EQUALS 13
-- 4(4): orders in a period between death and entitlement -> the figure as if the orders came into force before; otherwise NOTHING.
#ASSERT `sch 5 para 4(4) the amount of the increase to which W is entitled` TRUE TRUE 12 13 EQUALS JUST 13
#ASSERT `sch 5 para 4(4) the amount of the increase to which W is entitled` TRUE FALSE 12 13 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `sch 5 para 4(4) the amount of the increase to which W is entitled` FALSE TRUE 12 13 EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `Paragraph 5 to 7`

-- 7(3): both (a) and (b) -> falls within; either missing -> does not.
#ASSERT `sch 5 para 7(3) the woman falls within this sub-paragraph` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 5 para 7(3) the woman falls within this sub-paragraph` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `sch 5 para 7(3) the woman falls within this sub-paragraph` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- 5(1): (a), (b) and (b)(i) or (ii).
#ASSERT `sch 5 para 5(1) this paragraph applies` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 5 para 5(1) this paragraph applies` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 5 para 5(1) this paragraph applies` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `sch 5 para 5(1) this paragraph applies` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- 5(2): which paragraph sets out the amounts.
#ASSERT `sch 5 para 5(2) the paragraph that sets out the amounts` `sch 5 test a widow who attained pensionable age in 2005` `sch 5 test a deceased husband` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `sch 5 para 5(2)(a) the amounts are set out in paragraph 5A`
#ASSERT `sch 5 para 5(2) the paragraph that sets out the amounts` `sch 5 test a widow who attained pensionable age in 2005` `sch 5 test a deceased wife` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `sch 5 para 5(2)(c) the amounts are set out in paragraph 6A`
#ASSERT `sch 5 para 5(2) the paragraph that sets out the amounts` `sch 5 test a widow who attained pensionable age in 2005` `sch 5 test a deceased wife` FALSE TRUE EQUALS `sch 5 para 5(2)(a) the amounts are set out in paragraph 5A`
#ASSERT `sch 5 para 5(2) the paragraph that sets out the amounts` `sch 5 test a widow who attained pensionable age in 2005` `sch 5 test a deceased wife` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `sch 5 para 5(2)(c) the amounts are set out in paragraph 6A`
#ASSERT `sch 5 para 5(2) the paragraph that sets out the amounts` `sch 5 test a widower` `sch 5 test a deceased wife` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `sch 5 para 5(2)(b) the amounts are set out in paragraph 6`
#ASSERT `sch 5 para 5(2) the paragraph that sets out the amounts` `sch 5 test a widower` `sch 5 test a deceased husband` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `sch 5 para 5(2)(c) the amounts are set out in paragraph 6A`
#ASSERT `sch 5 para 5(2) the paragraph that sets out the amounts` `sch 5 test a widow who attained pensionable age in 2005` `sch 5 test a deceased husband` FALSE TRUE EQUALS `sch 5 para 5(2)(a) the amounts are set out in paragraph 5A`
-- The surviving civil partner of a man: (c)(iii), paragraph 6A, whatever the sexes.
#ASSERT `sch 5 para 5(2) the paragraph that sets out the amounts` `sch 5 test a widow who attained pensionable age in 2005` `sch 5 test a deceased husband` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `sch 5 para 5(2)(c) the amounts are set out in paragraph 6A`

§§ `The paragraph after 7(3) -- the modification and the appropriate amount`

-- Expected: W entitled 5 Apr 2012 and S died 5 Apr 2012 -> applies. W entitled 6 Apr 2012 -> only if (6) (payment for an earlier period). S died 6 Apr 2012 -> no.
#ASSERT `sch 5 para after 7(3) the modification of paragraphs 5A to 6A applies` (Date 5 4 2012) FALSE (Date 5 4 2012) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 5 para after 7(3) the modification of paragraphs 5A to 6A applies` (Date 6 4 2012) FALSE (Date 5 4 2012) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `sch 5 para after 7(3) the modification of paragraphs 5A to 6A applies` (Date 6 4 2012) TRUE (Date 5 4 2012) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 5 para after 7(3) the modification of paragraphs 5A to 6A applies` (Date 5 4 2012) FALSE (Date 6 4 2012) EQUALS NOTHING
-- (5): the greater of (a) and (b): 12 and 15 -> 15; 20 and 15 -> 20; outside the modified cases the term is undefined -> NOTHING.
#ASSERT `sch 5 para after 7(3) the appropriate amount` (JUST TRUE) 12 15 EQUALS JUST 15
#ASSERT `sch 5 para after 7(3) the appropriate amount` (JUST TRUE) 20 15 EQUALS JUST 20
#ASSERT `sch 5 para after 7(3) the appropriate amount` NOTHING 20 15 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `sch 5 para after 7(3) the appropriate amount` (JUST FALSE) 20 15 EQUALS NOTHING
-- 5A: death 5 Oct 2002: 10/2 + 6 + 4 = 15; death 6 Oct 2002: 6/2 + 4/2 = 5; no appropriate amount: NOTHING.
#ASSERT `sch 5 para 5A the sum of the amounts` (Date 5 10 2002) 10 (JUST 6) 4 EQUALS JUST 15
#ASSERT `sch 5 para 5A the sum of the amounts` (Date 6 10 2002) 10 (JUST 6) 4 EQUALS JUST 5
#ASSERT `sch 5 para 5A the sum of the amounts` (Date 6 10 2002) 10 NOTHING 4 EQUALS NOTHING
-- 6, with the increase 20 (12 before April 1988, 8 after), appropriate 6, section 109 increases 1, any paragraph 5 increase 4:
-- death 5 Apr 1989: 20 + 6 + 4 = 30; 6 Apr 1989: 12 + 8/2 + (6 - 1) + 4 = 25; 5 Oct 2002: 25; 6 Oct 2002: 12/2 + 6/2 + 4/2 = 11.
#ASSERT `sch 5 para 6 the sum of the amounts` (Date 5 4 1989) 20 12 8 (JUST 6) 1 4 EQUALS JUST 30
#ASSERT `sch 5 para 6 the sum of the amounts` (Date 6 4 1989) 20 12 8 (JUST 6) 1 4 EQUALS JUST 25
#ASSERT `sch 5 para 6 the sum of the amounts` (Date 5 10 2002) 20 12 8 (JUST 6) 1 4 EQUALS JUST 25
#ASSERT `sch 5 para 6 the sum of the amounts` (Date 6 10 2002) 20 12 8 (JUST 6) 1 4 EQUALS JUST 11
#ASSERT `sch 5 para 6 the sum of the amounts` (Date 6 10 2002) 20 12 8 NOTHING 1 4 EQUALS NOTHING
-- 6A: 12/2 + 6/2 + 4/2 = 11.
#ASSERT `sch 5 para 6A the sum of the amounts` 12 (JUST 6) 4 EQUALS JUST 11
#ASSERT `sch 5 para 6A the sum of the amounts` 12 NOTHING 4 EQUALS NOTHING
-- 7(2) rounding.
#ASSERT `sch 5 para 7(2) the amount as rounded` 0.004 EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `sch 5 para 7(2) the amount as rounded` 0.005 EQUALS 0.01
#ASSERT `sch 5 para 7(2) the amount as rounded` 2.345 EQUALS 2.35
#ASSERT `sch 5 para 7(2) the amount as rounded` 2.3449 EQUALS 2.34
-- Paragraph 5 as a whole. A widow of a man who died 5 Oct 2002: 5A(2): 10/2 + 6 + 4 = 15.
#ASSERT `sch 5 para 5 the amount by which the rate of W’s pension is increased` `sch 5 test a widow who attained pensionable age in 2005` `sch 5 test a deceased husband` FALSE FALSE (Date 5 10 2002) TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE 10 6 4 (JUST 6) 1 4 EQUALS JUST 15
-- 5A(3), death 6 Oct 2002, appropriate 6, any increase 3.01: 3 + 1.505 = 4.505, rounded half up to 4.51.
#ASSERT `sch 5 para 5 the amount by which the rate of W’s pension is increased` `sch 5 test a widow who attained pensionable age in 2005` `sch 5 test a deceased husband` FALSE FALSE (Date 6 10 2002) TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE 10 6 4 (JUST 6) 1 3.01 EQUALS JUST 4.51
-- A widower of a woman who died 1 Jan 1989: 6(2): 20 + 6 + 4 = 30.
#ASSERT `sch 5 para 5 the amount by which the rate of W’s pension is increased` `sch 5 test a widower` `sch 5 test a deceased wife` FALSE FALSE (Date 1 1 1989) TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE 20 12 8 (JUST 6) 1 4 EQUALS JUST 30
-- A surviving civil partner: 6A: 12/2 + 6/2 + 4/2 = 11.
#ASSERT `sch 5 para 5 the amount by which the rate of W’s pension is increased` `sch 5 test a widow who attained pensionable age in 2005` `sch 5 test a deceased wife` TRUE FALSE (Date 1 1 2010) TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE 20 12 8 (JUST 6) 1 4 EQUALS JUST 11
-- Paragraph 5(1) not met -> NOTHING; the appropriate amount undefined -> NOTHING.
#ASSERT `sch 5 para 5 the amount by which the rate of W’s pension is increased` `sch 5 test a widow who attained pensionable age in 2005` `sch 5 test a deceased husband` FALSE FALSE (Date 5 10 2002) TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE 10 6 4 (JUST 6) 1 4 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `sch 5 para 5 the amount by which the rate of W’s pension is increased` `sch 5 test a widow who attained pensionable age in 2005` `sch 5 test a deceased husband` FALSE FALSE (Date 5 10 2002) TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE 10 6 4 NOTHING 1 4 EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `Paragraphs 7A, 7B, 7C`

-- 7A: 3C applies and the lump-sum election (made or treated) -> entitled; the increase election, or 3C not shown to apply -> NOTHING.
#ASSERT `sch 5 para 7A(2) W is entitled to a widowed person’s or surviving civil partner’s lump sum` (JUST TRUE) (JUST `sch 5 para 3C(2)(b) an election that paragraph 7A (the lump sum) applies`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `sch 5 para 7A(2) W is entitled to a widowed person’s or surviving civil partner’s lump sum` (JUST TRUE) (JUST `sch 5 para 3C(2)(a) an election that paragraph 4 (the increase of pension) applies`) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `sch 5 para 7A(2) W is entitled to a widowed person’s or surviving civil partner’s lump sum` NOTHING (JUST `sch 5 para 3C(2)(b) an election that paragraph 7A (the lump sum) applies`) EQUALS NOTHING
-- 7B(1): S deferred from 1 Jan 2025 and died 1 Apr 2025: the period ended on 31 Mar 2025 (a Monday); prescribed day Monday -> 31 Mar to 6 Apr 2025.
#ASSERT `sch 5 para 7B(1) the last accrual period beginning during the period before S’s death` 1 (Date 1 1 2025) (Date 1 4 2025) EQUALS JUST (Period WITH `the first day` IS Date 31 3 2025, `the last day` IS Date 6 4 2025)
#ASSERT `sch 5 para 7B(1) the lump sum before rounding` (JUST 5.5) EQUALS JUST 5.5
#ASSERT `sch 5 para 7B(1) the lump sum before rounding` NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
-- 7B(3) P: basic 100 and half of additional 40 = 120.
-- The accrued amount's formula is omitted from this text, as in 3B(3): the function answers NOTHING whatever A, P and R are.
#ASSERT `sch 5 para 7B(3) the accrued amount for an accrual period` 0 100 6 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `sch 5 para 7B(3) the accrued amount for an accrual period` 50 120 6 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `sch 5 para 7B(3) P, the amount of pension for the accrual period` 100 40 EQUALS 120
-- 7B(3) R, (4), (5), (6): as paragraph 3B.
#ASSERT `sch 5 para 7B(3) the percentage rate R` 3 NOTHING EQUALS JUST 5
#ASSERT `sch 5 para 7B(3) the percentage rate R` 3 (JUST 4) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `sch 5 para 7B(4) the day a change in the base rate is treated as taking effect` (Date 8 1 2025) 1 NOTHING EQUALS Date 13 1 2025
#ASSERT `sch 5 para 7B(5) the amount of pension counted for an accrual period` `sch 5 test a pension with every named increase` 4 EQUALS 104
#ASSERT `sch 5 para 7B(6) the increase under section 47(1) that is counted` 12 4 EQUALS 12
-- 7B(7).
#ASSERT `sch 5 para 7B(7) the lump sum after the orders` TRUE TRUE 9.5 EQUALS JUST 9.5
#ASSERT `sch 5 para 7B(7) the lump sum after the orders` TRUE FALSE 9.5 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `sch 5 para 7B(7) the lump sum after the orders` FALSE TRUE 9.5 EQUALS NOTHING
-- 7C(1) rounding of a lump sum: 12.345 -> 12.35; 12.3449 -> 12.34; 0.004 -> 0.
#ASSERT `sch 5 para 7C(1) the lump sum as rounded` 12.345 EQUALS 12.35
#ASSERT `sch 5 para 7C(1) the lump sum as rounded` 12.3449 EQUALS 12.34
#ASSERT `sch 5 para 7C(1) the lump sum as rounded` 0.004 EQUALS 0

§§ `Paragraph 8`

-- 8(5): an increase under section 51A(2) attributable to W's contributions is left out: 10 becomes 9; otherwise not covered.
#ASSERT `sch 5 para 8(5) the increase or lump sum to which W is entitled under paragraph 4(1A) or 7A(2)` TRUE 10 9 EQUALS JUST 9
#ASSERT `sch 5 para 8(5) the increase or lump sum to which W is entitled under paragraph 4(1A) or 7A(2)` FALSE 10 9 EQUALS NOTHING
-- 8(6): the letters W and S.
#ASSERT `sch 5 para 8(6) the meaning of the letter` `sch 5 para 8(6) the letter W` EQUALS "a widow, widower or surviving civil partner (W) who is entitled to a Category A or Category B retirement pension"
#ASSERT `sch 5 para 8(6) the meaning of the letter` `sch 5 para 8(6) the letter S` EQUALS "the other party to the marriage or civil partnership (S), who has died"
